<table border="0" cellpadding="5" width="550" cellspacing="5" height="400" >
<tr valign="top" height="400" >
<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; color:#000000; bEditID:r3st1; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<div style=""><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><b>Dear Client,</b><br><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;">Employees can make changes to their Insperity Group Health Plan coverage during their annual open enrollment period. If no changes are made during open enrollment, the employee’s current election — including an election of no coverage — will carry over to the next coverage period. If a coverage option is discontinued and no new election is made, employees will be moved to the closest comparable option at the new rates for their coverage tier.<br><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><b>Changes Outside Open Enrollment<br><br></b></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;">After open enrollment ends, employees may only change their elections if they experience a <b>Qualifying Life Event (QLE)</b>. Employees have <b>60 days from the event date</b> to request a change.<br><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><b>Examples of Qualifying Life Events include:</b></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><ul><li>Marriage, divorce, or legal separation</li><li>Beginning or ending a domestic partnership</li><li>Birth, adoption, or placement for adoption</li><li>Death of a dependent</li><li>Change in dependent or employee eligibility under another group health plan</li><li>Court order requiring coverage (QMCSO)</li><li>Change in residence that affects eligibility</li><li>Gaining or losing eligibility for Medicare, Medicaid, or CHIP</li><li>Enrollment in Marketplace coverage</li><li>Reduction in hours (less than 30 per week) with enrollment in other coverage</li><li>Other events permitted by the Plan</li></ul></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><b>Important:</b></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><ul><li><b>Enrollments and additions</b> (e.g., adding a spouse or newborn) are generally <b>retroactive to the event date</b> if requested within 60 days.</li><li><b>Terminations</b> are usually <b>prospective</b> (effective when the request is submitted), except for <b>death, divorce, or domestic partnership termination</b>, which remain retroactive.</li></ul></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><b>How to Submit a Mid-Year Change:</b></div><div style=""><ol style=""><li style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;">Go to <b>portal.insperity.com &gt; My Account &gt; Benefits &gt; Mid-Year Change</b> and click <b>Access Now.<br><br><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt=""><br><br></b></li><li style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;">Select <b>Submit Change.</b></li><li style=""><font face="arial"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Complete</span></font><b style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;">&nbsp;</b><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;">the online form, choosing the appropriate event type </span><font face="arial">(e.g., birth of a child = “Change in Number of Dependents”).</font></li><li style="">Answer all questions and click Submit to finalize.</li></ol><span style="font-size: 12pt;">No documentation is required during submission, but some events (e.g., QMCSO) may require follow-up documentation.</span><br style="font-size: 12pt;"><br style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Please share this information with employees who experience a qualifying event. Contact me with any questions.</span></div></div>]]></td>
</tr>
</table>